      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's crucial not to equate \"intellectual complexity\" exclusively with Western academic frameworks. While the Renaissance piece demonstrates high technical proficiency in illusionism, the complexity of the Sub-Saharan art lies in its deep, functional knowledge of cosmology, social structure, and symbolic language. Their sophistication is embedded in cultural meaning and performance, representing a conceptual mastery entirely different from mastering vanishing points. Therefore, they are not less complex, but simply operate within distinct, valid systems of knowledge.",
      "source": "target",
